WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.10 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Learning and adaptive management

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Learning turns evidence into better decisions, and shows you what works before you grow.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.170
Learning is the step that turns evidence into better decisions. Adaptive management means openly changing activities, targets or even your Theory of Change because of what you found.

4
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.170
Simple learning formats

5
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:37.500
After-action review: What was planned, what happened, why, and what we will do differently. For example: After the first market day: too few small loaves, so bake more next Saturday.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:49.570
Quarterly session: Time set aside to read data and feedback and ask “so what?” and “now what?” For example: Co-founders meet each quarter for two hours with the dashboard and feedback log.

7
00:00:49.570 --> 00:01:03.211
Lessons log: Each decision recorded with an owner and a date, then checked. For example: Start trainee shifts at 7 am, owner the baking lead, by 1 June: checked at the next review.

8
00:01:03.611 --> 00:01:04.211
Why it matters

9
00:01:04.211 --> 00:01:09.885
1. It is how you find out what works before you grow.

10
00:01:09.885 --> 00:01:14.819
2. Early on, changing course is expected, not a failure.

11
00:01:14.819 --> 00:01:20.752
3. Decisions that are written down actually get carried out.

12
00:01:21.152 --> 00:01:21.752
What it changes

13
00:01:21.752 --> 00:01:26.315
1. Your monitoring and evaluation findings become decisions here.

14
00:01:26.315 --> 00:01:32.359
2. Your Theory of Change and targets, revised openly when evidence says so.

15
00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:38.293
3. Your reports: what you changed and why builds credibility.

16
00:01:38.693 --> 00:01:39.293
What to avoid

17
00:01:39.293 --> 00:01:44.226
Collecting data but never making time to discuss it.

18
00:01:44.226 --> 00:01:48.419
Hiding disappointing findings instead of using them.

19
00:01:48.419 --> 00:01:55.833
Changing course without those who need to agree, such as co-founders or funders.

20
00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:58.233
You plan your learning routine and record a first review.

21
00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:02.233
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:06.833
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
